# Custom Exception Design Guide
## When to Create Checked vs Unchecked Exceptions in Contract Management

---

## 🎯 **Decision Framework**

### **Use Custom CHECKED Exceptions when:**
- ✅ **Recoverable conditions** that calling code should handle
- ✅ **Expected business scenarios** in normal operation
- ✅ **External system failures** (temporary/recoverable)
- ✅ **Caller can take meaningful action** to resolve

### **Use Custom UNCHECKED Exceptions when:**
- ❌ **Programming errors** or bugs in logic
- ❌ **Business rule violations** (data integrity issues)
- ❌ **Configuration errors** or system setup problems
- ❌ **Conditions caller typically cannot recover from**

---

## 📋 **Custom CHECKED Exceptions - Contract Scenarios**

### **Scenario 1: Contract Approval Workflow**
```java
// Custom Checked Exception
public class ContractApprovalPendingException extends Exception {
    private final String contractId;
    private final String currentApprover;
    private final LocalDateTime pendingSince;
    
    public ContractApprovalPendingException(String contractId, String currentApprover, LocalDateTime pendingSince) {
        super("Contract " + contractId + " is pending approval from " + currentApprover 
              + " since " + pendingSince);
        this.contractId = contractId;
        this.currentApprover = currentApprover;
        this.pendingSince = pendingSince;
    }
    
    // Getters for recovery information
    public String getContractId() { return contractId; }
    public String getCurrentApprover() { return currentApprover; }
    public LocalDateTime getPendingSince() { return pendingSince; }
}

// Usage - Caller MUST handle this
public class ContractService {
    public void activateContract(String contractId) throws ContractApprovalPendingException {
        Contract contract = findContract(contractId);
        
        if (!contract.isApproved()) {
            throw new ContractApprovalPendingException(
                contractId, 
                contract.getCurrentApprover(),
                contract.getSubmittedForApproval()
            );
        }
        
        contract.setStatus(ContractStatus.ACTIVE);
    }
}

// Calling code - Must handle the exception
public class ContractController {
    public ResponseEntity<String> activateContract(@PathVariable String contractId) {
        try {
            contractService.activateContract(contractId);
            return ResponseEntity.ok("Contract activated successfully");
            
        } catch (ContractApprovalPendingException e) {
            // Recoverable - caller can take action
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.ACCEPTED)
                .body("Contract pending approval from " + e.getCurrentApprover() 
                     + ". Please follow up or wait for approval.");
        }
    }
}
```

### **Scenario 2: External System Integration**
```java
// Custom Checked Exception
public class ContractValidationServiceUnavailableException extends Exception {
    private final String serviceUrl;
    private final int retryAfterSeconds;
    
    public ContractValidationServiceUnavailableException(String serviceUrl, int retryAfterSeconds, Throwable cause) {
        super("Contract validation service at " + serviceUrl + " is temporarily unavailable. Retry after " 
              + retryAfterSeconds + " seconds.", cause);
        this.serviceUrl = serviceUrl;
        this.retryAfterSeconds = retryAfterSeconds;
    }
    
    public String getServiceUrl() { return serviceUrl; }
    public int getRetryAfterSeconds() { return retryAfterSeconds; }
}

// Usage
public class ExternalValidationService {
    public ValidationResult validateContract(Contract contract) 
            throws ContractValidationServiceUnavailableException {
        try {
            return httpClient.post(validationEndpoint, contract);
        } catch (ConnectTimeoutException | HttpServerErrorException e) {
            // Temporary failure - caller can retry
            throw new ContractValidationServiceUnavailableException(
                validationEndpoint, 30, e);
        }
    }
}

// Calling code
public class ContractProcessor {
    public void processContract(Contract contract) {
        try {
            ValidationResult result = validationService.validateContract(contract);
            // Process normally
            
        } catch (ContractValidationServiceUnavailableException e) {
            // Recoverable - schedule retry
            logger.warn("Validation service unavailable: {}", e.getMessage());
            scheduleRetry(contract, e.getRetryAfterSeconds());
        }
    }
}
```

### **Scenario 3: Business Rule Conflicts**
```java
// Custom Checked Exception
public class ContractConflictException extends Exception {
    private final List<String> conflictingContractIds;
    private final ConflictType conflictType;
    
    public enum ConflictType {
        OVERLAPPING_DATES, DUPLICATE_VENDOR, EXCLUSIVE_TERRITORY
    }
    
    public ContractConflictException(ConflictType conflictType, List<String> conflictingContractIds) {
        super("Contract conflict detected: " + conflictType + " with contracts: " + conflictingContractIds);
        this.conflictType = conflictType;
        this.conflictingContractIds = new ArrayList<>(conflictingContractIds);
    }
    
    public List<String> getConflictingContractIds() { return new ArrayList<>(conflictingContractIds); }
    public ConflictType getConflictType() { return conflictType; }
}

// Usage
public class ContractConflictChecker {
    public void checkForConflicts(Contract newContract) throws ContractConflictException {
        List<Contract> existing = findOverlappingContracts(newContract);
        
        if (!existing.isEmpty()) {
            List<String> conflictIds = existing.stream()
                .map(Contract::getContractId)
                .collect(Collectors.toList());
                
            throw new ContractConflictException(
                ConflictType.OVERLAPPING_DATES, conflictIds);
        }
    }
}

// Calling code
public class ContractCreationService {
    public String createContract(ContractRequest request) {
        try {
            Contract contract = new Contract(request);
            conflictChecker.checkForConflicts(contract);
            return contractRepository.save(contract).getContractId();
            
        } catch (ContractConflictException e) {
            // Recoverable - user can resolve conflicts
            throw new BusinessConflictException(
                "Cannot create contract due to conflicts with: " + 
                String.join(", ", e.getConflictingContractIds()) +
                ". Please review and modify dates or terms."
            );
        }
    }
}
```

