## 🚫 **Custom UNCHECKED Exceptions - Contract Scenarios**

### **Scenario 1: Business Rule Violations (Programming Errors)**
```java
// Custom Unchecked Exception
public class InvalidContractStateException extends RuntimeException {
    private final String contractId;
    private final ContractStatus currentStatus;
    private final ContractStatus attemptedStatus;
    
    public InvalidContractStateException(String contractId, ContractStatus currentStatus, 
                                       ContractStatus attemptedStatus) {
        super("Invalid state transition for contract " + contractId + 
              ": cannot change from " + currentStatus + " to " + attemptedStatus);
        this.contractId = contractId;
        this.currentStatus = currentStatus;
        this.attemptedStatus = attemptedStatus;
    }
    
    // Getters for debugging
    public String getContractId() { return contractId; }
    public ContractStatus getCurrentStatus() { return currentStatus; }
    public ContractStatus getAttemptedStatus() { return attemptedStatus; }
}

// Usage - Programming error, caller cannot recover
public class Contract {
    public void setStatus(ContractStatus newStatus) {
        // Business rule: TERMINATED contracts cannot be reactivated
        if (this.status == ContractStatus.TERMINATED && 
            newStatus == ContractStatus.ACTIVE) {
            throw new InvalidContractStateException(
                this.contractId, this.status, newStatus);
        }
        
        this.status = newStatus;
    }
}

// This is a programming error - calling code should prevent this
public class ContractService {
    public void reactivateContract(String contractId) {
        Contract contract = findContract(contractId);
        
        // BUG: Should check if contract is terminated first!
        contract.setStatus(ContractStatus.ACTIVE); // May throw InvalidContractStateException
    }
}
```

### **Scenario 2: Data Integrity Violations**
```java
// Custom Unchecked Exception
public class ContractDataIntegrityException extends RuntimeException {
    private final String contractId;
    private final String violationType;
    private final String fieldName;
    
    public ContractDataIntegrityException(String contractId, String fieldName, String violationType) {
        super("Data integrity violation in contract " + contractId + 
              ": " + violationType + " in field '" + fieldName + "'");
        this.contractId = contractId;
        this.fieldName = fieldName;
        this.violationType = violationType;
    }
    
    public String getContractId() { return contractId; }
    public String getFieldName() { return fieldName; }
    public String getViolationType() { return violationType; }
}

// Usage
public class ContractValidator {
    public void validateContractData(Contract contract) {
        // This should never happen if application logic is correct
        if (contract.getStartDate().isAfter(contract.getEndDate())) {
            throw new ContractDataIntegrityException(
                contract.getContractId(), 
                "startDate/endDate", 
                "Start date is after end date"
            );
        }
        
        // This indicates a serious bug in the application
        if (contract.getValue().compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) < 0) {
            throw new ContractDataIntegrityException(
                contract.getContractId(),
                "value",
                "Negative contract value"
            );
        }
    }
}
```

### **Scenario 3: Configuration Errors**
```java
// Custom Unchecked Exception  
public class ContractConfigurationException extends RuntimeException {
    private final String configKey;
    private final String expectedFormat;
    
    public ContractConfigurationException(String configKey, String expectedFormat, String actualValue) {
        super("Invalid configuration for '" + configKey + "'. Expected: " + expectedFormat + 
              ", but got: '" + actualValue + "'");
        this.configKey = configKey;
        this.expectedFormat = expectedFormat;
    }
    
    public String getConfigKey() { return configKey; }
    public String getExpectedFormat() { return expectedFormat; }
}

// Usage
public class ContractNumberGenerator {
    private String contractPrefix;
    
    @PostConstruct
    public void initialize() {
        contractPrefix = environment.getProperty("contract.id.prefix");
        
        // Configuration error - should be fixed before deployment
        if (contractPrefix == null || !contractPrefix.matches("[A-Z]{3}")) {
            throw new ContractConfigurationException(
                "contract.id.prefix",
                "3 uppercase letters (e.g., 'CNT')",
                contractPrefix
            );
        }
    }
}
```

